# Normalise line endings.
#
# Eight source files were rewritten CRLF by a Windows tool and showed up as
# 2,096 changed lines that were not changes at all — every line "modified" by
# its ending alone. That noise hides real edits in review and creates conflicts
# between machines. Git now stores LF and checks out LF everywhere.
#
# LF is also required rather than cosmetic for the files below: a shell script
# or Dockerfile with CRLF endings fails inside a Linux container with errors
# like "/bin/sh^M: bad interpreter".
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries git must never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Generated; collapse it in diffs so a dependency bump does not bury a review.
frontend/package-lock.json linguist-generated=true -diff
